# --- CYBERPUN-16-1-t2: asset-pack extraction scratch (OUTSIDE the catalog) ---
# Unpacking the attached asset pack lands all 33 pack entries at once, so the
# zip is always extracted into one of these repo-root scratch dirs and the
# wanted files are then `git mv`d into their own `<name>.imageset/` folder.
#
# Deliberately NOTHING under CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/ is ignored:
#   * the committed asset set is defined POSITIVELY -- every file inside the
#     catalog is tracked and belongs to exactly one imageset (22 PNGs, one per
#     imageset, bare `filename` in its own Contents.json). It is no longer
#     defined by subtraction, so a new or corrected sheet dropped into the
#     catalog can never be silently skipped by `git add`;
#   * `actool` compiles the catalog from DISK, not from git, so unpacking into
#     the catalog and hiding the surplus behind ignore rules produces local
#     warnings/errors (unassigned content) that CI never reproduces. Extract
#     here instead, never inside `Assets.xcassets/`.
#
# Never-imported pack entries (docs/bootstrap.md "Explicitly deferred") --
# `assets/screens/` UI mockups, `tileset_structure.png`, and the buildings/
# duplicates -- are simply never moved out of scratch, so no ignore rule has
# to carry that decision.
/tmp_assets_extract/
/tmp_probe/
